<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1539" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ag-gĕmo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adg-</span></b> ), ĕre, v.
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
			groan</i>, <i>wail</i>, <i>lament</i>
			at a thing; <i>absol.</i> or with dat.
			(only <b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adgemit Alcides,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					5, 400</span></i>
			, where Riese has <i>Et gemit</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adgemit et nostris ipsa carina malis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tr. 1, 4, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uterque loquenti adgemit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 11, 247</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
